ACTION REQUIRED BEFORE FIRST PUBLIC COMMIT

This file currently contains only the BSL parameters block. The canonical
Business Source License 1.1 legal text has NOT been reproduced here, because
licence text should be copied verbatim from the authoritative source rather
than transcribed.

Before publishing this repository:

  1. Copy the full BSL 1.1 text from https://mariadb.com/bsl11/
  2. Paste it below this notice, keeping the parameters block above intact
  3. Fill in the Licensor name — see the note on entity ownership below
  4. Delete this "ACTION REQUIRED" section

Two further items to settle before the repository becomes public:

  - ENTITY OWNERSHIP. Decide who the Licensor is: an individual or a company.
    If this work is intended to be sold, keep it clearly separate from any
    employer's accounts, equipment and time, so ownership of the intellectual
    property is unambiguous. Worth a short conversation with a solicitor
    before the first public commit rather than after.

  - CONTRIBUTOR LICENCE AGREEMENT. Put a CLA in place before accepting the
    first external pull request. Under BSL this matters more than it would
    under a permissive licence: as licensor you need the rights to offer
    commercial licences covering the whole codebase, and to later extract
    contributor-written code into the planned Apache 2.0 library. A DCO
    sign-off alone does not grant those rights.

See docs/DECISIONS.md entry 012 for the full reasoning behind this choice.
